[SO-34512848] Q: SpringMVC XML error- Randomly
A: <p>This kind of issue:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>cvc-elt.1: Cannot find the declaration of element 'beans'.
  root-context.xml /SwiftEmploymentMVC/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/spring
  line 3 XML Problem</p>
</blockquote>

<p>generally is a <strong>dependency one</strong>, that is caused by some <strong>missing classes</strong>, themselves caused by using <strong>conflicting dependencies versions</strong>.
Even if you say everything is fine with your Apache server, you are using <strong>too much different versions for your Spring jars</strong>.</p>

<p>By example, you use <code>spring-security-core</code> in version <code>3.1.0.RELEASE</code>, but <code>spring-security-config</code> in version <code>4.0.3.RELEASE</code>.
Those jars are linked, and you are using 2 different major versions, which could be a problem.</p>

<p>If you don't know <strong>which dependencies versions are required by a jar</strong>, have a look at <a href="http://mvnrepository.com/" rel="nofollow">http://mvnrepository.com/</a>.<br>
It lists the different required dependencies by type.</p>

<p>If your case, I would suggest that you use your <code>org.springframework-version</code> property for more (or all) of your Spring jars.</p>


