<p>Better to create a custom class, extending from something like <code>JPanel</code> and override it's <code>paintComponent</code> method and perform your custom painting there (and call <code>super.paintComponent</code> before you do any custom painting)</p>

<p>See <a href="http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/java/painting-140037.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Painting in AWT and Swing</a> and <a href="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/uiswing/painting/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Performing Custom Painting</a> for more details</p>

