Q: Why it is an error to ignore a rejected promise on Chrome?
A: <p>Rejecting a promise basically means something bad happened, and that you should be handling it with a call to <code>catch</code>. If you reject a promise without having a <code>catch</code>, it will throw an exception (more accurately, an unhandled rejection) </p>

<pre><code>var a = (new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {
    reject("my error")
})).catch((err) =&gt; {
    console.error(err)
})
</code></pre>

<p>I'm guessing it is a specificity of V8 if this happens only under Chrome, but it makes sense to me</p>

