Q: Jquery check if i tag has a class and replace it
A: <p>First of all, make sure your class names do NOT have spaces. Spaces in <code>class="a b"</code> actually means 2 separate classes, a and b, not a class "a b". Also as others have mentioned, IDs should be unique. So with code:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;ul class="list-inline recommended-logo"&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;i id="icon-changer-1" class="first_class"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;First class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;i id="icon-changer-2" class="second_class"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Second class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;i id="icon-changer-3" class="third_class"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Third, class&lt;/span&lt;/li&gt;
   &lt;li&gt;&lt;i id="icon-changer-4" class="fourth_class"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Four class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>You can select by class (with a .) and replace easily:</p>

<pre><code>$('.first_class').removeClass('first_class').addClass('fifth_class')
