Q: Spring Boot app configuration with DB2 database
A: <p>To work with Spring Boot and embedded in-memory database, such as H2, you need just to add its dependency to your project:</p>

<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
   &lt;groupId&gt;com.h2database&lt;/groupId&gt;
   &lt;artifactId&gt;h2&lt;/artifactId&gt;
   &lt;scope&gt;runtime&lt;/scope&gt;--&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>and, for example, Spring Data JPA starter:</p>

<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.boot&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-boot-starter-data-jpa&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Then Spring Boot will make the rest of autoconfiguring itself.</p>

<p>Thus you can start to work with your entities, eg:</p>

<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@Entity
public class MyEntity {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue
    private Integer id;

    // other stuff
}
</code></pre>

<p>And repositories:</p>

<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>public interface MyEntityRepo extends JpaRepository&lt;MyEntity, Integer&gt; {
}
</code></pre>

<p>Additional info: </p>

<ul>
